# Compose

## Recomposition Optimization

### @Immutable for UI state

Annotate `data class` UI state types with `@Immutable` so Compose treats them as stable:

```kotlin
@Immutable
data class GuidesViewState.Display(
    val heroSearchValue: String,
    val guides: List<GuideUI>,
    val imageResources: ImageResources,
)
```

Strong skipping mode is already enabled in `composeApp/build.gradle.kts` (`composeCompiler { enableStrongSkippingMode = true }`). Even so, prefer `@Immutable` for clarity and forward compatibility.

### rememberUpdatedState for callbacks inside effects

```kotlin
@Composable
private fun WatchGuideSelection(onSelect: (String) -> Unit) {
    val currentOnSelect by rememberUpdatedState(onSelect)
    LaunchedEffect(Unit) { /* use currentOnSelect() */ }
}
```

### derivedStateOf for derived state

```kotlin
val showScrollToTop by remember {
    derivedStateOf { lazyListState.firstVisibleItemIndex > 0 }
}
```

### key in LazyColumn

Always:

```kotlin
LazyColumn {
    items(items = guides, key = { it.matchId }) { guide -> GuideItemView(guide) }
}
```

## Composable Splitting

### Pass minimum required data

```kotlin
// ✅
GuideItemView(
    heroName = guide.heroName,
    role = guide.role,
    icon = imageResources.heroes[guide.heroId],
)

// ❌
GuideItemView(guide = guide, imageResources = imageResources)
```

This keeps the recomposition surface small and the composable testable.

### Modifier as the first optional parameter

Required composable parameter shape:

```kotlin
@Composable
internal fun GuideItemView(
    heroName: String,
    role: MatchPlayerPositionType,
    modifier: Modifier = Modifier,
)
```

### Effects at the top of the composable

`LaunchedEffect`, `DisposableEffect`, `SideEffect` go before UI content. Extract complex effects into separate `@Composable private fun` helpers (no UI).

## Preview Rules

Every reusable composable in `features/.../ui/views/` should have a `@Preview` in the same file:

- Name: `Preview` + composable name (e.g., `PreviewGuideItemView`).
- `@Preview(showBackground = true)`.
- Wrapped in the project theme (`D2BuildHelperTheme { ... }` — see `theme/Theme.kt`).
- For multi-state composables, render variants in a `Column { ... }`.
- `private fun` — previews never leak as public API.

## Design System

### D2BuildHelperTheme — only source of tokens

Access colors, typography, and shapes via `D2BuildHelperTheme.colors` / `.typography` / `.shapes`. Never read from `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` or `MaterialTheme.typography` directly in feature UI code — the colorScheme mapping in `Theme.kt` is a safety net, not the primary mechanism.

### D2* wrappers for M3 components

Commonly used Material3 components (`Button`, `TextField`, `Chip`, `ProgressIndicator`, `IconButton`, `ModalBottomSheet`, …) must have a `D2*` wrapper in `:shared:common-ui` that explicitly maps all color slots from `D2BuildHelperTheme`. Use the wrapper at call sites in `feature-*/ui/`. Never use bare M3 components in feature UI modules without a wrapper.

When adding a new M3 component to a feature: stop, create the `D2*` wrapper in `common-ui`, then use it at the call site in the same commit.

### No hardcoded strings or colors

- String literals in `Text("...")` are forbidden — use moko-resources (`stringResource(MR.strings.x)`).
- `Color(0x...)` / `Color(0xFF...)` literals are forbidden — use DS tokens via `D2BuildHelperTheme.colors`.

## CompositionLocals

`LocalImageLoader` is the only CompositionLocal in the project. Do not introduce new ones without good reason — they hide dependencies and complicate testing.

## Local-mirror text inputs

When a text field is bound to a Store-side value with any latency between keystroke and state update (debounced filtering, async pipelines, MVI round-trip), mirror the value locally inside the composable to keep rendering instant:

```kotlin
var input by remember(externalValue) { mutableStateOf(externalValue) }
OutlinedTextField(
    value = input,
    onValueChange = {
        input = it
        onValueChange(it)   // propagate to Store/VM
    },
    /* ... */
)
```

`remember(externalValue)` reseeds local state when the Store-side value changes underneath us (programmatic resets). When the Store catches up to the typed value, `remember` reseeds to the same value — no visible glitch.

Used in `HeroFilterDialog`; apply the same pattern for any future text field with similar Store-round-trip latency.
